  takeaways: ['IP = logical address (DHCP assigns, DNS translates names); MAC = hardware address; switches forward within a LAN; routers connect networks; VLANs segment.', 'OSI layers 1–7: Physical, Data Link, Network, Transport, Session, Presentation, Application. Start troubleshooting at Layer 1.', 'HL7 v2 and FHIR exchange clinical data; DICOM handles images; PACS stores them.', 'CIA triad: confidentiality, integrity, availability; segmentation, patching, unique passwords and secure remote access protect devices.', 'MDS2 and SBOMs inform purchases; section 524B requires cybersecurity for new cyber devices; HIPAA Security Rule protects ePHI.'],
